From ee7270eed4e0ea1fa7e7f115f55c1a10b8869514 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:52:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(wire): cut DXF arcs and circles as true arcs

A selected DXF chain with an arc, a circle or a small joint gap is cut
on its own lines and arcs (wire_edm::wire_contour_arcs): concentric
arcs, pivot arcs at outside corners, trims at inside corners, and named
refusals for an arc under the kerf radius, a consumed parallel, a neck
and a joint gap over 0.25 um. The lead enters at the nearest path point
(towards +X from the centre of a circle); full circles cut as two half
arcs. The motion laws read the drawing exactly; the sim verifier reads
vertical arc moves as 25 nm chords against a waste-side product ring.
TEXT, MTEXT and DIMENSION entities no longer block a selected-chain
wire cut and are counted on the path. Exact straight polygons keep the
polygon path byte for byte. Goldens: ISO, Sodick and G-EDM for a die
circle and a line-and-arc punch.

Refs #3215
Fixes #3937

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
